A.4 YUBI gripper hardware design (CERN-OHL-W-2.0)

    YUBI (Yielding Universal Bidigital Interface), developed by Frontier
    Research Center, Toyota Motor Corporation.
    Source Location: https://github.com/Toyota/yubi-hw
    Copyright 2026 Toyota Motor Corporation
    Licence: CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal
    (CERN-OHL-W-2.0, section F)
    Paper: T. Ohkawa et al., "YUBI: Yielding Universal Bidigital Interface
    for Bimanual Dexterous Manipulation at Scale", arXiv:2606.10244, 2026.

    The following files are derived from the YUBI Gripper (DYNAMIXEL) design
    and its Franka mounting parts. This repository treats them as modified
    Covered Source: they are licensed under CERN-OHL-W-2.0, not under the
    Apache License 2.0 of this repository's code:

    - robosuite_env/assets/yubi_left/ and robosuite_env/assets/yubi_right/:
      the visual meshes (visual/, visual_mj/), the collision meshes (coll/,
      coll_mj/, coll_mj_hulls/, guard_collision/) and manifest.json, for
      the left and right gripper, and
      robosuite_env/assets/yubi_guard_collision_manifest.json, the record
      of the generated collision guards.
    - robosuite_env/assets/fr3_yubi_right_registered/: the YUBI attachment
      and flange meshes that mount the gripper on the FR3 (visual/ and
      collision/) and manifest.json.

    Modification notice (CERN-OHL-W-2.0 section 3.3(b)). Modified by AIRoA:
    - yubi_left/ and yubi_right/ (made on 2026-07-06 and
      2026-07-05): each assembled gripper COLLADA scene
      (YUBI_Gripper_DYNAMIXEL_{left,right}_use_assembled.dae, recorded as
      source_dae in manifest.json; not part of this repository) was split
      into 60 per-part OBJ meshes, re-exported for MuJoCo, and given CoACD
      convex collision parts.
    - yubi_left/guard_collision/ and yubi_right/guard_collision/ (added on
      2026-08-25): 102 convex exterior collision guards per hand, generated
      from those meshes by robosuite_env/tools/build_yubi_full_collision.py
      (docs/yubi_guard_collision.md).
    - fr3_yubi_right_registered/ (added on 2026-08-01): the attachment and
      flange meshes were placed in the YUBI physical-root frame of the FR3
      mount chain recorded in manifest.json, and given CoACD convex
      collision parts.
    Recipients of this repository receive these modified files directly,
    so section 3.3(c) does not require a separate Source Location Notice
    for them while they are conveyed here.

    Written by AIRoA and used with the files above:
    - robosuite_env/assets/yubi_left.xml and yubi_right.xml, the MuJoCo
      models that load the meshes above and place the finger hinges at the
      servo output shafts of the design;
    - robosuite_env/robots/yubi/, the gripper model, calibration and
      controller. The servo torque constant in
      control/configs/spec_nominal.yaml is derived from the DYNAMIXEL
      XM430-W350-R datasheet.
    The meshes keep their CERN-OHL-W-2.0 licence when these files load them.

    None of the CERN-OHL-W-2.0 files above is in the sdist or wheel:
    pyproject.toml ships only robosuite_env/assets/wrist_rgb_calibration.json
    from assets/.


